= addr-bare-word-is-not-a-session
f lib/mux-addr_lib
t mux-addr
# A BARE WORD IS A SESSION, which is the grammar's whole ergonomic claim:
# the common case costs nothing and the RARE field carries the delimiter.
# Dropping the no-dot arm leaves the session empty for every bare name, so
# every caller addressing `api` would act on a whole partition instead.
