= resume-address-drops-the-session
f bin/mux
t mux-resume
# The session half of the one-argument address. Losing it makes every
# addressed resume rebuild the set and land nowhere, which looks like success
# and is the `mux latch box` bug this package already shipped once: a default
# that succeeded at the wrong thing and said nothing.
-   rs_focus=$MUX_ADDR_SESS
+   rs_focus=
