# THE HOTTEST PATH MUST NOT LEAK. The render runs per client every
# status-interval, and it used anonymous mktemp files with an EXIT-only
# trap, which does NOT run when the shell is signalled. Once leaked, a
# /tmp/tmp.XXXXXXXXXX cannot be told from any other program s, so
# nothing can ever prune it. A deterministic name is bounded instead.
# ... and a persistent name has to be TRUNCATED, because the records
# file is appended to: otherwise the strip accumulates every session on
# every tick for as long as the client lives. This is the one new way
# the fix can be wrong, which is why it has its own record.
