# THE CONFIG'S COMMENT RULE HAS ONE HOME, and this reader did not use it: its
# own sed dropped a full-line comment and left an INLINE one in the value. Not
# cosmetic, because the value is EXECUTED (context-command) or parsed as a
# list of variable names (env-ready), where the stray `#` reads as a name
# nothing manages, `mux resume` exits 2, ssh-classify calls that `refused`,
# and a latch gives up for ever on a box that is fine.
