# THE PARTITION IS AN ARGUMENT, and that is the whole risk of lifting these
# out of bin/mux: they read the global `$part` there, which happened to hold
# the right value in the one file that set it. A lib still reaching for a
# caller's variable works in that file and answers about nothing anywhere
# else. The set is keyed BY partition, so the wrong one answers about another
# partition's sessions, which is an isolation boundary crossed silently.
